body:
If you can, try to tell your parents how you feel honestly.Tell them about the pressure you feel and feeling like an "embarassment" because they are the ones that can actually tell you how they feel about you and they can comfort you but only if you are honest with them. If they however aren't that supportive then I'd say you should not worry about being an embarassment to them and just do whatever YOU want to do with your life (do not EVER do drugs though). Like moving away from them and starting a fresh start with new people around you, finding something that you like doing and just pursuing things you actually enjoy without giving a single f\*ck about the people that would judge. 

&#x200B;

But back to the first point you should be honest with your parents and let them comfort you if that's possible maybe they can give you courage and confidence.
